---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import pilot from '../content/pilot.json';
import { newQuestions, screenedPaperCount } from '../lib/newQuestions';
const { result: r, question: q, run_id } = pilot;
const scores = r.scores.spring_initialized;
---
<Base title="A question worth testing">
  <section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">FIELD NOTE 001 / CLIMATE SCIENCE</p><h1>Open questions.<br /><em>Visible evidence.</em></h1><p class="lede">A small research observatory that turns a question into a plan, a bounded experiment, and a result you can inspect.</p><a class="button" href="/questions/Q-ENSO-001/">Explore the pilot <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="orbit" aria-hidden="true"><div class="ring r1"></div><div class="ring r2"></div><div class="ring r3"></div><span class="dot"></span><span class="orbit-label">OBSERVE<br />QUESTION<br />TEST<br />REPRODUCE</span><span class="coordinates">05°N–05°S / 170°W–120°W</span></div></section>
  <section class="intro-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE INVESTIGATION</p><h2>Can calendar information improve spring El Niño forecasts?</h2><p>The spring predictability barrier remains a research challenge. We tested whether a fixed, season-aware model improves six-month Niño 3.4 predictions on observations beyond its training period.</p><p class="muted">No answer to this exact comparison was located in the documented search. This limited search does not certify novelty.</p></div><aside class="finding"><span class="badge">{r.claim_supported_under_frozen_rule ? 'BOUNDED SUPPORT' : 'NO ROBUST ADVANTAGE DEMONSTRATED'}</span><h3>{r.claim_supported_under_frozen_rule ? 'The frozen rule was met.' : 'The frozen rule was not met.'}</h3><p>{r.claim_supported_under_frozen_rule ? 'The measured benefit passed the prespecified checks in this retrospective sample.' : 'A completed experiment can leave a question open. The proposed improvement did not pass every prespecified check.'}</p><a href={'/research/'+run_id+'/'}>Read the full result ↗</a></aside></section>
  <section class="metrics" aria-label="Primary experiment summary"><div><strong>{scores.seasonal_ar6.n}</strong><span>Spring-initialized forecasts</span></div><div><strong>{scores.seasonal_ar6.rmse.toFixed(3)}<small> °C</small></strong><span>Season-aware model RMSE</span></div><div><strong>6<small> months</small></strong><span>Fixed prediction lead</span></div><div><strong>2</strong><span>Fresh container executions</span></div></section>
  {newQuestions.length>0 && <section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">CROSS-DISCIPLINARY PILOTS</p><h2>More questions. Bounded attempts.</h2><p>{screenedPaperCount} papers screened across {new Set(newQuestions.flatMap(q=>q.disciplines)).size} disciplines produced {newQuestions.length} source-linked question cards. Each record shows its search coverage and practical blockers.</p>{newQuestions.filter(q=>q.report_run_id).map(q=><article class="question-card"><p class="eyebrow">{q.disciplines.join(' / ')}</p><h3><a href={'/research/'+q.report_run_id+'/'}>{q.title}</a></h3><p>{q.outcome_summary}</p></article>)}<a class="text-link" href="/questions/">Browse all questions ↗</a></section>}
  <section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">TRACE THE EVIDENCE</p><h2>Every step leaves a record.</h2></div><a href="/methodology/">How the pilot works ↗</a></div><ol class="pipeline"><li><span>01</span><h3>Source</h3><p>A 2026 paper describes persistent spring forecast limitations.</p></li><li><span>02</span><h3>Scope</h3><p>A narrow comparison, documented literature search, fixed decision rule.</p></li><li><span>03</span><h3>Test</h3><p>NOAA observations, two trained models and one persistence baseline.</p></li><li><span>04</span><h3>Reproduce</h3><p>The same output regenerated in a fresh, restricted Linux container.</p></li></ol></section>
  <section class="closing"><p class="eyebrow">WHAT THIS RECORD MEANS</p><h2>Computation is one layer of evidence.</h2><p>This is an AI-assisted pilot with computational checks. The operator accepted its bounded negative interpretation. Independent scientific assessment and external review have not occurred. The wider ENSO problem remains open.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about/">Read the scope and limitations ↗</a></section>
</Base>
